All deterministic gates pass. Highlights:

- Structure-aware guesses: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Track B reference algorithm: 8/8 successes, 9,405,614 exact operations across eight instances.
- Compact invariant route: 245 operations, verified 20/20.
- Canonical-key invariance: 60/60; unrelated diversity: 20/20.
- Answer: 35 atoms, 166 worst-case characters.

The only incomplete requirement is external oracle certification. All three harness runs stopped before receiving a model response because OpenRouter returned HTTP 403, “Key limit exceeded (total limit).” The transcripts correctly record infrastructure errors, so this result should not be submitted as hardened until the key limit is resolved and the three runs are repeated.
